From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 20:12:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] inset box-shadow: isolate the shadow group so DestOut can't
 erase the page

vello_cpu's needs_buf() only allocates a layer buffer for non-default
blend, opacity, mask or filter; a layer with Mix::Normal, opacity 1.0
and a clip is optimized into a bare clip that draws straight onto the
backdrop. The inset-shadow construction relied on that outer layer
isolating its Compose::DestOut child, so the blurred DestOut blob
composited against the canvas. It erased the element's own background
(and everything beneath) instead of trimming the shadow fill, so an
inset shadow stack rendered as a transparent hole with a dark glow.
Force the isolation buffer with an epsilon opacity, which still
composites at 255/255 in the u8 pipeline.

Also apply self.scale to the inset shadow offset, matching the outset
path.

The real upstream fix is an explicit isolation flag in vello's layer
API, or needs_buf considering nested destructive composes.
---
 src/render/box_shadow.rs | 15 ++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/render/box_shadow.rs b/src/render/box_shadow.rs
index 0e72820..25bc4d5 100644
--- a/src/render/box_shadow.rs
+++ b/src/render/box_shadow.rs
@@ -109,14 +109,23 @@ impl ElementCx<'_, '_> {
             // TODO draw shadows with matching individual radii instead of averaging
             let radius = self.frame.border_radii.average();
             let transform = self.transform.then_translate(Vec2 {
-                x: shadow.base.horizontal.px() as f64,
-                y: shadow.base.vertical.px() as f64,
+                x: shadow.base.horizontal.px() as f64 * self.scale,
+                y: shadow.base.vertical.px() as f64 * self.scale,
             });

+            // vello_cpu only buffers a layer with non-default blend /
+            // opacity / mask / filter; a bare clip layer draws straight
+            // onto the backdrop, so the nested Compose::DestOut below would
+            // erase the page under the element instead of trimming the
+            // shadow fill, punching a transparent hole through an inset
+            // shadow stack. The epsilon
+            // opacity forces the isolation buffer; the layer still
+            // composites at 255/255 alpha in the u8 pipeline.
+            const ISOLATE_OPACITY: f32 = 0.999_999;
             scene.push_layer(
                 Fill::NonZero,
                 Mix::Normal,
-                1.0,
+                ISOLATE_OPACITY,
                 self.transform,
                 &padding_box,
                 None,
